* PIC16(L)F1847 Pin Definitions -- 18-Pin PDIP/SOIC, 20-Pin SSOP,
* and 28-Pin QFN/UQFN/VQFN (combined)
* Source: Microchip DS40001453G "PIC16(L)F1847 Data Sheet,
*         18/20/28-Pin Flash Microcontrollers", Pin Diagrams section
*         and Table 1-2 (Pinout Description).
*
* Primary device: PIC16F1847 -- determines this file's name.
*
* Companion device -- PIC16LF1847 (low-voltage variant) differs only
* in operating voltage range/speed grade, same as every other "L"
* variant handled in this project (e.g. ATmega32 vs ATmega32L). The
* datasheet itself is written as "PIC16(L)F1847" throughout, i.e. one
* unified document covering both. Both included:
*   PIC16F1847, PIC16LF1847
*
* Package scope -- ALL THREE packages (18-pin PDIP/SOIC, 20-pin SSOP,
* 28-pin QFN/UQFN/VQFN) are combined into this single file. Confirmed
* directly against the datasheet's own Pin Diagrams and Table 1
* (18/20/28-PIN SUMMARY): every package exposes the exact same 16
* signal pins -- RA0-RA7, RB0-RB7 -- plus VDD/VSS. The ONLY
* differences between packages are:
*   - 18-pin: one VDD, one VSS (16 signal pins + 2 power = 18)
*   - 20-pin: adds a second VDD and a second VSS (duplicate power
*     pins only, no new signals) -> 20
*   - 28-pin QFN/UQFN/VQFN: same duplicated VDD/VSS as the 20-pin
*     package, plus 6 NC (no-connect) pins simply filling out the
*     larger QFN body -> 28
* Per this project's established handling (duplicate VCC/GND pins
* collapse to a single V/G record regardless of package -- see the
* ATmega32 28-pin QFN precedent), and NC pins need no record at all,
* this is a clean, fully justified combination -- there is no
* pin-count-driven functional difference to scope around here, unlike
* the ATmega/dsPIC cases where larger packages added genuinely new
* GPIO or analog pins. The 28-pin QFN/UQFN/VQFN variants also have an
* exposed bottom pad the datasheet recommends tying to VSS -- not a
* distinct signal, already covered by the G record.
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   RA5     -- MCLR/VPP/SS1. Datasheet lists this pin's primary
*             function as "General purpose I/O" (same row format as
*             every other port pin), consistent with the MCLRE
*             config bit allowing RA5 to be used as ordinary GPIO
*             when the dedicated Reset function is disabled.
*             Classified B (not I) per this project's established
*             convention for config-bit-gated dual-function pins.
*   RA6/RA7 -- OSC2/CLKOUT/... and OSC1/CLKIN/..., oscillator-mode-
*             dependent alternate functions on otherwise ordinary
*             GPIO pins (external clock/crystal mode is a config-bit
*             choice, not a pin dedication). Classified B for their
*             default GPIO role, same reasoning as dsPIC33CK's
*             RB0/RB1 OSCI/OSCO.
*   RB6/RB7 -- possible datasheet naming inconsistency: the RB6 pin-
*             name header lists "T1OSI" (Timer1 Oscillator Input),
*             but Table 1-2's own function breakdown for RB6 lists
*             "T1OSO" (Timer1 Oscillator Output) -- the same "T1OSO"
*             name Table 1-2 also gives RB7. Recorded as T1OSI for
*             RB6 (trusting the pin-name header, and matching the
*             expected T1OSI/T1OSO crystal-pair convention) -- verify
*             against a second source (e.g. the family reference
*             manual) before relying on this if Timer1 async
*             oscillator mode matters for your use case.
*   RB0-RB7 -- all individually support interrupt-on-change with an
*             individually enabled weak pull-up; a shared electrical
*             feature of the whole port, not a separate alternate
*             function requiring its own field.
*
* All other pins (RA0-RA4, RB0-RB5 aside from the notes above) are
* ordinary GPIO pins with ADC/comparator/capacitive-sensing/PWM/
* USART/SPI/I2C alternate functions, many relocatable via the
* APFCON0/APFCON1 Alternate Pin Function registers. Classified B.

D PIC16(L)F1847 18/20/28-Pin PDIP/SOIC/SSOP/QFN/UQFN/VQFN 8-bit Flash Microcontroller
P PIC16F1847 PIC16LF1847

V VDD
B RA0 AN0/CPS0/C12IN0-/SDO2
B RA1 AN1/CPS1/C12IN1-/SS2
B RA2 AN2/CPS2/C12IN2-/C12IN+/VREF-/DACOUT
B RA3 AN3/CPS3/C12IN3-/C1IN+/VREF+/C1OUT/CCP3/SRQ
B RA4 AN4/CPS4/C2OUT/T0CKI/CCP4/SRNQ
B RA5 MCLR/VPP/SS1
B RA6 OSC2/CLKOUT/CLKR/P1D/P2B/SDO1
X 1
K SIMCLK

B RA7 OSC1/CLKIN/P1C/CCP2/P2A
B RB0 T1G/CCP1/P1A/INT/SRI/FLT0
B RB1 AN11/CPS11/RX/DT/SDA1/SDI1
B RB2 AN10/CPS10/MDMIN/TX/CK/SDA2/SDI2/SDO1
B RB3 AN9/CPS9/MDOUT/CCP1/P1A
B RB4 AN8/CPS8/SCL1/SCK1/MDCIN2
B RB5 AN7/CPS7/P1B/TX/CK/SCL2/SCK2/SS1
B RB6 AN5/CPS5/T1CKI/T1OSI/P1C/CCP2/P2A/ICSPCLK
B RB7 AN6/CPS6/T1OSO/P1D/P2B/MDCIN1/ICSPDAT
G VSS
